1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:27,040
Oh, you've got to be kidding.

2
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:38,040
What kind of battle do you have to wage to end up like this?

3
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:39,040
Is that...

4
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,040
Everyone!

5
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,040
I found them!

6
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:45,040
They're over here!

7
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:47,040
You positive?

8
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,040
They defeated them?

9
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:52,040
Two upper-ranked demons?

10
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:54,040
Master Kaguya!

11
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,040
One hundred years.

12
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,040
It took one hundred years for something to finally change.

13
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:01,040
And it actually happened.

14
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,040
Don't you see?

15
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:05,040
This must be an omen.

16
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:09,040
Fate is about to take a dramatic turn for us.

17
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:12,040
The effects will be widespread.

18
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:15,040
Everything will be shaken to its core.

19
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:20,040
And eventually, he will feel it as well.

20
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,040
Mozan Kibutsuji.

21
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,040
We will defeat you.

22
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:28,040
Our generation will put an end to you without fail.

23
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,040
And then you, the sole blemish of my family, will be gone.

24
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,040
Oh, no!

25
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,040
Ah!

26
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,040
Oh!

27
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:36,040
Oh!

28
00:01:36,040 --> 00:02:06,020
To be continued...

29
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:36,020
To be continued...

30
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:47,040
The alternate dimension...

31
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:49,040
The Infinity Castle...

32
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:53,040
The fact I was summoned here can only mean one thing...

33
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,640
They managed to kill an upper rank!

34
00:02:55,640 --> 00:03:05,640
The Infinity Castle...

35
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:08,640
The Infinity Castle...

36
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:10,640
The Infinity Castle...

37
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,640
The Infinity Castle...

38
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,640
The Infinity Castle...

39
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:28,640
The Infinity Castle...

40
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:29,140
No!

41
00:03:58,640 --> 00:03:59,640
No!

42
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:12,640
Oh!

43
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:45,640
Well, well, well, if it isn't Lord Arkazor!

44
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:58,640
How lovely it is to see you in such good health!

45
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:02,640
What has it been 90 years since I last saw your face?

46
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:13,640
When I was summoned here, I thought for a second you might have perished and my heart began to sing.

47
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:19,640
My poor worried heart was filled with anguish at the thought of it.

48
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,640
How terrifying, terrifying!

49
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:32,640
It appears that in the time we've been apart you've even forgotten so much as how to count, Kyoko!

50
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:38,640
It's been 113 years since we were last summoned.

51
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,640
That's an indivisible number.

52
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,640
An uneven number!

53
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:44,640
And it's odd.

54
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:45,640
Terrifying!

55
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,640
Terrifying!

56
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:48,640
Biwa woman!

57
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,640
Has Lord Muzan arrived yet or not?

58
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:55,640
I can say with certainty he has not.

59
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,640
Then what about Upper One?

60
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,640
Is he here?

61
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:02,640
Don't tell me it was him who somehow got killed.

62
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,640
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

63
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:11,640
You're beginning to hurt my feelings here, Lord Akaza.

64
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,640
Weren't you even a little concerned about me?

65
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:20,640
Here I was worried sick something might have happened to you.

66
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:26,640
After all, you're a cherished comrade of mine, and I'd be heartbroken if I lost any of my comrades.

67
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,640
Greetings, Lord Doma.

68
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:30,640
Hi, Kyoko.

69
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:31,640
Long time no see.

70
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:32,640
Is that a brand new pot?

71
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,640
It's beautiful.

72
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,640
Remember the one you gave me?

73
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,640
I'm using it to display a woman's head.

74
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:36,640
Fits perfectly.

75
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:37,640
I never intended were it to be used like that.

76
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,640
Though I must say I'm intrigued.

77
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,640
You'd love it.

78
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:40,640
You should come to my place sometime.

79
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,640
Get it off.

80
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:42,640
Hm?

81
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,640
Get your hand off of me.

82
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,640
Ahhhhh hog!

83
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,640
addictiveва�뀙ed Battersea Doma

84
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,640
sins flickers

85
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:50,640
taught the ladder

86
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,640
if to dig some scol раз

87
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,560
in the city to sometimes

88
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,560
Oh got it.

89
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:57,640
You should come to my place sometime.

90
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:59,080
Get it off.

91
00:06:59,080 --> 00:06:59,600
Hm?

92
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,600
Get your hand off of me.

93
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:03,600
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

94
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,640
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

95
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:09,600
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

96
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:19,880
Wow, that was quite a punch.

97
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:23,960
Unless I'm mistaken, you've gotten slightly stronger.

98
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,680
You asked about Upper One earlier.

99
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,520
He's the first one I summoned.

100
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,500
In fact, he's been here all along.

101
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:45,320
I've been here the entire time.

102
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:51,220
It seems Lord Muzan has arrived.

103
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,480
Wait for the game.

104
00:07:53,480 --> 00:08:04,360
...

105
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:25,320
Gyutaro is no longer with us, meaning the upper ranks are now incomplete.

106
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:46,480
Oh, is that true, my lord? No, you have my sincerest apologies. Since I was the one who brought Gyutaro in, how can I atone for this embarrassment? Let's see, I can gouge an eye out. Or maybe...

107
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:49,520
Keep your wretched eyeballs. I have no need for them.

108
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:58,860
I knew that Gyutaro would be defeated. As expected, Daki proved to be his weakness.

109
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:08,120
Had he just fought alone from the start, he most assuredly would have won.

110
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:13,480
If the battle hadn't gone on after he'd poisoned them...

111
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:19,920
Oh, well. None of it matters anymore.

112
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,820
How worthless.

113
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:36,080
Can't you see you're falling in order of who has the most of their humanity remaining?

114
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:42,240
But I guess that's fine. It's nothing new.

115
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:46,000
I've come to learn that I should expect nothing from you.

116
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:56,820
You're saying such tragic things again, but think about it.

117
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:01,820
Really? Has there ever been a time I didn't meet your expectations, my lord?

118
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:09,260
For starters, you have yet to annihilate the Ubuyashiki family.

119
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,600
And whatever became of the blue spider lily?

120
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:28,320
Centuries have passed, and you have nothing to show for it.

121
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,360
Answer me this.

122
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:37,760
Why do you exist if your sole purpose has become to disappoint me?

123
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:48,800
No! Please forgive us! I beg of you, I beg of you!

124
00:10:48,800 --> 00:11:00,720
I have nothing to say in response. However, Ubuyashiki is a master at evading us.

125
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:08,160
I'm afraid detective work isn't my strong point, either. I'm at my wit's end here.

126
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:13,200
Pardon me, Lord Muzan, but I have something for you.

127
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:18,080
You see, I've acquired some juicy information that I think will interest you.

128
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:22,000
Information that can change everything just a mere moment ago.

129
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:26,880
Have I ever told you lot how much I detest change?

130
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:35,760
Changes in circumstance. The changes of flesh. Changes in one's emotions.

131
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:41,920
Most changes cause only weakness and inferiority. And I am not weak.

132
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:49,600
What I'm interested in is permanence. To forever remain in perfect condition, immune to the disease of change.

133
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:59,360
To have none other than Lord Muzan's hand touching my head. How splendid. How sublime.

134
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:09,120
For the first time in over a century, an upper rank has been killed.

135
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,520
My frustration has reached its boiling point.

136
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:24,240
Don't ever give me unconfirmed information. And wipe that smirk off of your face.

137
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:36,240
I'd advise you all to act with more urgency from here on out.

138
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:42,320
I suppose you're not entirely at fault for your inadequacy. I've been too lenient with you because

139
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:47,360
you're upper ranks. Kyoko, once you've confirmed that information to be true,

140
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:50,560
you are to head over there with Han Tengu at once.

141
00:12:50,560 --> 00:13:02,720
Yes. Understood, my lord.

142
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:14,800
Oh, that's hardly fair. I'm the one who got the information in the first place. How annoying is that?

143
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:18,720
What? But that's what makes it intriguing.

144
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:25,840
Lord Gyoko, what kind of information do you have?

145
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:32,400
I'd like to tag along. But that wouldn't be...

146
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:39,760
You can tell little old me. I won't tell anyone.

147
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:47,840
I don't remember hearing Lord Muzan give you orders back there.

148
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:50,080
Get lost.

149
00:13:56,400 --> 00:14:01,120
Akaza. You always go too far.

150
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:06,720
It's all right, Lord Kokushibo.

151
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,320
I don't mind in the slightest.

152
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,240
It's not for your benefit that I chose to speak.

153
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,960
He disrupts the hierarchy.

154
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,560
Which, in turn, gives heed to insubordination among the ranks.

155
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:24,400
It's unacceptable.

156
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:31,760
Oh, I see.

157
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:40,800
Akaza. If you're unsatisfied with the ranks, then why not back up your words and challenge him to a battle?

158
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:45,280
Come on. Cut him some slack. He's just messing around.

159
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:50,400
You know as well as I do, if he were to challenge us, he'd only embarrass himself.

160
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:53,040
Look, he's just angsty, that's all.

161
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:58,000
Probably because I became a demon after him, and still got promoted before him.

162
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:02,480
I'd be upset too if I were in his shoes. Don't be so hard on him.

163
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:09,200
And I mean, besides, I didn't dodge his attack on purpose.

164
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:14,720
It's harmless horseplay. This is just our little way of nurturing our friendship.

165
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:20,080
Those of us on top shouldn't be giving our subordinates a hard time, don't you think?

166
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:20,960
Akaza.

167
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:32,000
From here on out, you are to show some respect. Do you understand?

168
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:39,040
Oh, I understand.

169
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:46,320
I understand. I'm going to kill you if it's the last thing I do.

170
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:56,800
Is that so? Then I wish you the best.

171
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:15,360
I don't know how, but I feel like I got shut out of that entire conversation.

172
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:18,320
Oh, but that's okay. I'm used to it.

173
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,600
Wait, Lord Akaza!

174
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,360
Hey, I wasn't done talking.

175
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:36,400
Please send Han Tengu and myself to the same location as fast as possible!

176
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:43,360
Biwa lady, send me two!

177
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:52,400
Hello? I know you can hear me!

178
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,520
You're free to join me down here if you want!

179
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,080
I respectfully decline.

180
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:07,760
Oh, you guys are always so cold to me.

181
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:13,840
Lord Founder, your disciples have just arrived.

182
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:17,600
Oh, is that right? Well, let's not keep them waiting.

183
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:22,720
All right. I just need to put this on and I'll be ready.

184
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:27,440
That's much better. You can send them in now.

185
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:32,400
I've brought you some tea.

186
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,760
Right. Thank you.

187
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:39,920
Aww. He's sound asleep.

188
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:45,360
Thanks for watching him. My wife's fast asleep in the other room.

189
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:51,200
I really must apologize. I feel bad making our guest babysit.

190
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:55,840
No, it's fine. She must be exhausted.

191
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:59,360
Giving birth and raising a child is no easy task.

192
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:09,280
I will be leaving after this. I don't want to overstay my welcome. That's all.

193
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:16,400
Please, sir. You saved our lives that day. If it hadn't been for you, I wouldn't be here,

194
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,080
nor would this child have been born.

195
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:29,040
Very well. Then the least I can do is pass down your name for posterity.

196
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:29,840
There's no need.

197
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:35,680
But, sir, didn't you say you were at a loss because you had no heirs?

198
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:40,400
Look, I know I'm just a charcoal merchant, but it's better than nothing.

199
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:44,080
Thank you, Sumiyoshi. But there's no need.

200
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:52,160
Those who have mastered their skills share the same fate. They always have.

201
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:58,320
They wind up in the same place, no matter what era they find themselves in.

202
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:02,160
And if lost, they'll find their way back.

203
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:10,400
Sumiyoshi, you seem to think of me as some kind of extraordinary person. But I'm really not.

204
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:17,040
I failed to protect everything that was important to me.

205
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:22,080
And throughout my life, I was unable to accomplish any of my goals.

206
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:26,400
My name is as worthless as I am.

207
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:32,640
Please, sir. Don't say something like that.

208
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:37,840
Please, I'm begging you. Don't talk about yourself that way.

209
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:42,400
It's so sad. So sad.

210
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:56,640
It was a dream.

211
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:09,440
Am I... alive?

212
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:17,840
Are you okay? You've been out for two months, ever since your last battle.

213
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:21,840
Really? Two months?

214
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:24,160
I see.

215
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:32,320
Thank goodness. We were so worried.

216
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:50,720
My name is Goto, and I'm a Kakashi. Basically, I'm a member of the Demon Slayer Core cleanup Squad.

217
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:54,960
Back when Tanjiro Kamado first met the Hashira, someone said to him,

218
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,760
Are you gonna sleep all day? Wake the hell up, will you?

219
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,120
That was me.

220
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,880
Fate has a way of bringing us together.

221
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:07,920
I found him and his friends two months ago in the entertainment district.

222
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:13,120
Since they were found like this, I figured they had to be close.

223
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:18,320
Each one of them suffered critical wounds and was unresponsive.

224
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:25,280
They might be younger than me, but they had the courage to become swordsmen, and so for that they have my respect.

225
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:29,280
Except for this guy. What's his deal?

226
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:35,680
Anyway, fast forward to now, and I'm delivering some mouth-watering Castella.

227
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:40,640
I gotta be honest, it's taking everything in me not to gobble it all up myself.

228
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:44,240
I would if it weren't a gift for our unconscious friend.

229
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:48,720
They say his sense of smell is so good that it just might...

230
00:21:57,360 --> 00:22:01,040
She better be over there contemplating how she's gonna clean up this mess that she made.

231
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,640
Oh, who am I kidding? She's probably off in la-la land.

232
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:07,440
Can you tell she grew up slaying demons instead of doing chores?

233
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:14,800
It's not like I can scold her. She's ranked higher than me. So here I am at 23, picking up her mess.

234
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:20,800
Pardon me, but I have some Castella here for him. You'll need to clear it away after a while.

235
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:23,360
But if it seems like it's going to go bad, feel free to eat it.

236
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,880
Oh, thank you very much.

237
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:35,760
Hey, when did he wake up from his coma? And why didn't you tell anyone?

238
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:42,080
You really are scatterbrained, you know that? You should have called for someone, or say he's woken up.

239
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:43,920
You idiot!

240
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:50,160
Seniority doesn't mean a thing right now, not in this case. I'll handle this myself.

241
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:52,160
Oh, thank you very much!

242
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:53,120
Kyo!

243
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:54,080
Sumi!

244
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,120
Gahou!

245
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:56,800
Aoi!

246
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,200
Tadjiro just woke up from his coma!

247
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:08,240
Thank goodness, you're okay!

248
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:10,080
Here, you can have my crackers.

249
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:12,400
Why is there Castella on the bed?

250
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,040
Oh, man.

251
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:20,160
Oh my gosh, it's a ghost!

252
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:27,280
Oh, good! It was just Miss Allie tangled up in all the laundry!

253
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:34,400
I was worried you were never going to wake up, and I felt bad because you went in my place. I'm sorry.

254
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:42,000
It's fine, really. What about the others? Are they all okay?

255
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:46,240
Was it the yellow-haired kid who left the other day?

256
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:46,560
Yep!

257
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:51,840
Yeah, he's fine. He's already back out on a mission. Against his will, of course.

258
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:55,120
He's tough. He was up and out of bed the very next day!

259
00:23:57,360 --> 00:24:01,440
That's nothing compared to the sound, Hashira. He and his wives just walked off.

260
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,640
Man, this really sucks!

261
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:11,600
The kakshi were dumbfounded by his strength. He was inhuman. In a way, it was scary.

262
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:15,600
How is he walking around? His injuries should have him hospitalized!

263
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:17,840
It's scary to think people like that exist.

264
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,160
I see.

265
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:22,800
And Inosuke?

266
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:26,240
Mr. Inosuke? He was on the brink of death.

267
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:35,120
It's true. Mr. Inosuke fought for his life, but there was too much poison in his body for his breathing to deal with it all.

268
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:43,280
Mr. Okay. So then, I guess I'm hallucinating right now, because I see him on the ceiling.

269
00:24:43,280 --> 00:24:49,840
Mr. How are you doing that?

270
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:53,520
How'd you notice me, Kanpachiro?

271
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:57,920
Well, uh, it helps him lying down.

272
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:04,320
It is I, the man who blessed to death and still woke up before you!

273
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:06,480
You sure did.

274
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:08,480
Man, Inosuke.

275
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,240
You're amazing.

276
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:17,200
You got that right! I'm not a weakling like you! Screw you for making us worry!

277
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:21,920
He's not weak, you're just different, Mr. Inosuke! Lady Shinobu said so!

278
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:26,080
Oh, Mr. Tanjiro! It's related to Mr. Inosuke!

279
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:30,640
It's a weasel called a honey badger from another country!

280
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:35,200
Their hide is so thick, it's like armor! Even lions can't bite their way through it!

281
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:36,800
It's so cute!

282
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:41,200
They're also poison-proof, which allows them to eat venomous snakes!

283
00:25:41,760 --> 00:25:42,160
Wow!

284
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:46,640
Lady Shinobu said Mr. Inosuke's like the honey badger!

285
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,760
The honey badger might be smarter.

286
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:50,400
Yeah.

287
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:54,000
Or maybe she just got tired of thinking about him.

288
00:25:55,840 --> 00:25:57,440
Will you get off of him?

289
00:25:57,440 --> 00:25:59,840
In other words, I'm so strong, I'm immortal!

290
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,760
Yeah, right. More like an idiot.

291
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:05,840
Who are you calling an idiot, you idiot?

292
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:09,200
Hi! Well, then you stop it, please!

293
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:10,880
Come on, let go!

294
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:14,960
Poison might not affect too much, but neither does any of the medicine we tried!

295
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:16,960
So you need to learn to be more careful!

296
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:23,020
Bob, please try to keep it down

297
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:28,540
Don't you rise to sleep, so please be quiet!

298
00:26:28,740 --> 00:26:30,840
Erommt?

299
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:33,880
Argh! He went back into a coma!

300
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:36,980
Would you mind not saying ominous stuff like that?

301
00:26:36,980 --> 00:26:38,980
Just be quiet, please.

302
00:26:38,980 --> 00:26:39,980
I have an idea.

303
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:41,980
We should cook him up some rice gruel.

304
00:26:43,980 --> 00:26:45,980
Let's just hope he recovers soon

305
00:26:45,980 --> 00:26:48,980
so he can work up an appetite for everything that we make.

306
00:27:06,980 --> 00:27:19,980
A week after he woke up, Mr. Tanjiro was back up on his feet.

307
00:27:22,980 --> 00:27:25,980
When we told Mr. Goto, who was on an expedition,

308
00:27:25,980 --> 00:27:28,980
he was stunned by the speed of his recovery.

309
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:33,980
You've got to be kidding me. They're all like this?

310
00:27:33,980 --> 00:27:37,980
Mr. Inosuke returned to duty soon after Mr. Tanjiro recovered.

311
00:27:37,980 --> 00:27:39,980
Watch out, everybody!

312
00:27:40,980 --> 00:27:42,980
Jezap, coming through!

313
00:27:42,980 --> 00:27:46,980
No, please! It's too cold!

314
00:27:46,980 --> 00:27:51,980
I'm scared! I just wanna go home!

315
00:27:51,980 --> 00:27:53,980
Come on, please!

316
00:27:53,980 --> 00:27:57,980
As for Mr. Zenitsu, he's still out on that mission far away from here.

317
00:27:57,980 --> 00:28:00,980
His fellow Corps members say he's driving them insane.

318
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:04,980
Miss Aoi! You... you just remembered me!

319
00:28:04,980 --> 00:28:06,980
You miss me? Do you miss me?

320
00:28:06,980 --> 00:28:08,980
You do miss me, don't you?

321
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:10,980
That's enough!

322
00:28:11,980 --> 00:28:16,980
As for Mr. Tanjiro, he's been doing his rehabilitation training every day without fail.

323
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:25,980
Ouch!

324
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:32,980
How cruel! Even after all this time, I still feel weak!

325
00:28:32,980 --> 00:28:39,980
Hey, Geo! While I was sleeping, did a new sword come? You know, to replace the one that I chipped!

326
00:28:39,980 --> 00:28:44,980
Did you say a sword? Sorry, no!

327
00:28:44,980 --> 00:28:50,980
You got letters from Mr. Haganesuka! Would you like to see them?

328
00:28:50,980 --> 00:28:54,980
I have no sword for the likes of you!

329
00:28:54,980 --> 00:28:57,980
Oh, wow! This is bad!

330
00:28:57,980 --> 00:28:59,980
It is, isn't it?

331
00:29:05,980 --> 00:29:09,980
Two months have already gone by, but we never received any sword!

332
00:29:12,980 --> 00:29:15,980
Oh, I know I messed up, but I only chipped it this time!

333
00:29:16,980 --> 00:29:18,980
Last time I snapped it in half!

334
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:23,980
Hmm... It's not your fault swords are bound to eventually get damaged.

335
00:29:24,980 --> 00:29:27,980
Mr. Haganesuka just happens to be a bit unforgiving.

336
00:29:28,980 --> 00:29:30,980
Why don't you just go to the village and talk to him?

337
00:29:31,980 --> 00:29:34,980
I'm sure he'd understand if you spoke to him in person!

338
00:29:35,980 --> 00:29:36,980
The village?

339
00:29:36,980 --> 00:29:38,980
The village where all the swordsmiths live.

340
00:29:39,980 --> 00:29:40,980
Huh? I can go?

341
00:29:49,980 --> 00:29:55,980
Pleasure to meet you. The Masters granted your approval for entry. I'll be guiding you there.

342
00:29:56,980 --> 00:30:00,980
Nice to meet you. I'm Tanjiro Kamado. Thank you for taking me.

343
00:30:01,980 --> 00:30:06,980
As your guide, I cannot tell you my name, but know I look forward to serving you.

344
00:30:07,980 --> 00:30:08,980
Put these on.

345
00:30:09,980 --> 00:30:10,980
What are they?

346
00:30:11,980 --> 00:30:13,980
A blindfold and earplugs. The village is hidden.

347
00:30:13,980 --> 00:30:17,980
Also, I'm afraid I'll need to carry you on my back.

348
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:19,980
What?

349
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:22,980
And since you have an acute sense of smell, you'll need these.

350
00:30:24,980 --> 00:30:26,980
Have a safe journey!

351
00:30:27,980 --> 00:30:33,980
The Swordsmith Village is where Nichiren's swords are forged, and so it's a vital place for the Demon Slayer Corps.

352
00:30:34,980 --> 00:30:38,980
In order to protect it from demon attacks, its whereabouts must be kept secret.

353
00:30:39,980 --> 00:30:42,980
Which is why no one knows the location of the village.

354
00:30:44,980 --> 00:30:46,980
Not even the lady taking me knows where it is.

355
00:30:48,980 --> 00:30:52,980
After traveling a certain distance, I'm passed on to a different Kakushi.

356
00:30:53,980 --> 00:30:57,980
And if that wasn't enough, both the routes and the Kakushi are frequently changed up.

357
00:30:58,980 --> 00:31:02,980
The only reason the Kakushi know where to go next is because they're guided by crows.

358
00:31:03,980 --> 00:31:05,980
Even the crows get switched up to keep things secret.

359
00:31:06,980 --> 00:31:08,980
Please be careful on your way back!

360
00:31:10,980 --> 00:31:11,980
What a good kid.

361
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:16,980
I'm told the mansion where the Master lives is somehow hidden in an even more complex way.

362
00:31:17,980 --> 00:31:20,980
Geez, smart people are incredible!

363
00:31:21,980 --> 00:31:22,980
Here we are.

364
00:31:22,980 --> 00:31:23,980
Here we are!

365
00:31:32,980 --> 00:31:33,980
Wow!

366
00:31:44,980 --> 00:31:45,980
Wow!

367
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:46,980
These buildings are amazing!

368
00:31:46,980 --> 00:31:50,980
Everyone says the same thing their first time here.

369
00:31:51,980 --> 00:31:55,980
I know that smell. There must be a hot spring nearby.

370
00:31:56,980 --> 00:32:00,980
Yes, that's quite impressive. You're more than welcome to go there if you'd like.

371
00:32:01,980 --> 00:32:06,980
But first, you're gonna want to turn left at the end of the street and go to the Chief's home.

372
00:32:07,980 --> 00:32:09,980
It's best you greet him before doing anything else.

373
00:32:10,980 --> 00:32:11,980
Right.

374
00:32:11,980 --> 00:32:13,980
I have to go, but I wish you the best.

375
00:32:13,980 --> 00:32:14,980
Thank you, and travel safe!

376
00:32:14,980 --> 00:32:28,980
Huh? Did I just hear an echo of gratitude?

377
00:32:28,980 --> 00:32:40,980
That means someone else is here! My heart's racing to no help!

378
00:32:40,980 --> 00:32:58,980
I'm glad you made it here safely. My name is Techin Techi Kawahara and I'm the Chief of this village. Nice to meet you!

379
00:32:58,980 --> 00:33:08,980
I might be the smallest person in this village, but I'm also the most important. Now, if you don't mind, I'd like to see the quality of the bow you used to show respect.

380
00:33:12,980 --> 00:33:15,980
I'm Tanjiro Kamado. It's a privilege to meet you!

381
00:33:16,980 --> 00:33:21,980
Oh my, what a fine young man. Please, help yourself to some sweets.

382
00:33:22,980 --> 00:33:23,980
Thank you very much, sir.

383
00:33:25,980 --> 00:33:26,980
These are delicious!

384
00:33:26,980 --> 00:33:27,980
Indeed.

385
00:33:28,980 --> 00:33:37,980
Oh, I know you're here for Hotaru, but unfortunately, he's gone missing. It's nothing to worry about, though. We'll soon find him.

386
00:33:38,980 --> 00:33:39,980
Hotaru?

387
00:33:39,980 --> 00:33:41,980
That's right. Hotaru Haganesuka.

388
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:43,980
That's such a cute name!

389
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:50,980
Isn't it? I'm actually the one who named him. He thinks it's too cute and resents me for naming him that.

390
00:33:51,980 --> 00:33:52,980
Oh, I'm so sorry.

391
00:33:52,980 --> 00:34:01,980
That boy's behaved like that ever since he was a child. As quickly as he loses his temper, he vanishes. I apologize.

392
00:34:01,980 --> 00:34:06,980
Please don't! After all, it's my fault. I'm the one who's breaking my sword.

393
00:34:07,980 --> 00:34:08,980
No, you're wrong.

394
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:14,980
He's the one who forged a faulty sword, so it's his fault and only his fault.

395
00:34:14,980 --> 00:34:21,980
As soon as he's found, we'll apprehend him. You have my word.

396
00:34:22,980 --> 00:34:23,980
Good. Good.

397
00:34:23,980 --> 00:34:26,980
You aren't gonna hurt him, right?

398
00:34:27,980 --> 00:34:33,980
More importantly, I hear that you still haven't quite recovered enough to start hunting demons again.

399
00:34:34,980 --> 00:34:40,980
And as such, if you don't have a sword by the time you're well, I will assign someone else to be your swordsmith.

400
00:34:40,980 --> 00:34:49,980
Speaking of healing, our hot springs works wonders on aches and injuries. You should go. Your body will thank you for it.

401
00:34:50,980 --> 00:34:51,980
I'll show you the way.

402
00:34:54,980 --> 00:34:55,980
I hope everything will be okay.

403
00:34:55,980 --> 00:35:08,980
They are foundries and workshops just like this one all over the village.

404
00:35:11,980 --> 00:35:14,980
The swords you all use are made exactly like that.

405
00:35:18,980 --> 00:35:23,980
You all work so hard just so that we have something to fight with. Thank you very much.

406
00:35:23,980 --> 00:35:27,980
Oh, please. It's our job. There's no need to thank us.

407
00:35:30,980 --> 00:35:34,980
You're in for a treat with this hot spring. It has all kinds of great healing properties.

408
00:35:35,980 --> 00:35:41,980
For bruises, cuts, burns, constipation, hemorrhoids, everything from gout to a broken heart.

409
00:35:42,980 --> 00:35:44,980
The hot spring will heal, and the path ahead will take you to it.

410
00:35:45,980 --> 00:35:46,980
Right.

411
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:49,980
I'll be down here, preparing your meal if you need anything.

412
00:35:50,980 --> 00:35:51,980
Yes. Thank you so much.

413
00:35:51,980 --> 00:35:57,980
Tanjiro, it's you! It really is you!

414
00:35:58,980 --> 00:36:05,980
Watch out! Please be careful! Your breasts aren't this close to spilling out!

415
00:36:05,980 --> 00:36:07,980
Listen! You've got some present to me!

416
00:36:07,980 --> 00:36:08,980
Watch out!

417
00:36:08,980 --> 00:36:12,980
Somebody ignored me up there just now! All I did was say hello and he ignored me!

418
00:36:12,980 --> 00:36:13,980
Well, who was it?

419
00:36:13,980 --> 00:36:19,980
I don't even know! I asked him his name but he ignored that too! Isn't that awful? And I'm a Hashira! All the good vibes I got from my mouth have been cancelled out!

420
00:36:19,980 --> 00:36:20,980
If it helps, dinner's gonna be ready soon. And it's Matsutake Rice!

421
00:36:20,980 --> 00:36:24,980
What?! Really?! We're having Matsutake Rice! We're having Matsutake Rice!

422
00:36:24,980 --> 00:36:25,980
I guess she's a hearty eater! We're having Matsutake Rice!

423
00:36:25,980 --> 00:36:26,980
We're having Matsutake Rice!

424
00:36:26,980 --> 00:36:27,980
Wow! It's massive!

425
00:36:27,980 --> 00:36:28,980
Ow!

426
00:36:28,980 --> 00:36:29,980
What is this? Hold on!

427
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:30,980
It's massive!

428
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:31,980
Ow!

429
00:36:31,980 --> 00:36:44,980
What is this? Hold on!

430
00:36:44,980 --> 00:36:46,980
I guess she's a hearty eater.

431
00:36:50,580 --> 00:36:52,580
Wow, it's massive!

432
00:36:56,580 --> 00:36:57,580
What is this?

433
00:36:58,080 --> 00:36:59,880
Hold on, it's a tooth!

434
00:37:06,480 --> 00:37:08,080
That mohawk-style haircut.

435
00:37:10,580 --> 00:37:13,780
Right, it's the guy whose name I heard from Sumi.

436
00:37:14,580 --> 00:37:15,980
Genyashina Zugawa!

437
00:37:17,680 --> 00:37:18,380
Die!

438
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:28,880
How have you been?

439
00:37:29,180 --> 00:37:32,380
I meant to ask, are you and the Wind Hashira related?

440
00:37:35,480 --> 00:37:37,980
Stop trying to make small talk with me, dammit!

441
00:37:37,980 --> 00:37:44,080
And here I thought for a second we could bond in our nakedness.

442
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:46,380
Making new friends sure is tough.

443
00:37:49,780 --> 00:37:51,580
Wow, that's impressive!

444
00:37:51,580 --> 00:37:53,380
You think so?

445
00:37:53,380 --> 00:37:55,680
But I really only nibbled, to be honest.

446
00:37:55,780 --> 00:37:57,880
I need to eat more to get stronger!

447
00:37:58,880 --> 00:37:59,680
Oh, right.

448
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:03,680
The guy you met at the hot spring was Genyashina Zugawa.

449
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:04,780
He's also a swordsman.

450
00:38:04,780 --> 00:38:05,880
What?

451
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:07,680
Did you say Shina Zugawa?

452
00:38:08,380 --> 00:38:10,680
That would make him the Wind Hashira's brother.

453
00:38:11,180 --> 00:38:12,980
But he didn't have a younger brother.

454
00:38:12,980 --> 00:38:14,080
He insisted.

455
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:16,280
Maybe they're on bad terms.

456
00:38:16,580 --> 00:38:17,880
How heart-wrenching.

457
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:19,380
You really think so?

458
00:38:19,980 --> 00:38:20,980
I wonder what happened.

459
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:26,180
What are you trying to say, Nezuko?

460
00:38:26,780 --> 00:38:28,180
Oh, I see!

461
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:32,780
I have four siblings in my family, and we all get along pretty well.

462
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:37,380
So it's hard for me to fathom what the Shina Zugawa brothers could be going through.

463
00:38:38,380 --> 00:38:40,880
Speaking of, Genya still hasn't shown up.

464
00:38:41,380 --> 00:38:43,380
I was hoping we could at least have a talk.

465
00:38:44,780 --> 00:38:46,480
I don't think he's coming at all.

466
00:38:47,080 --> 00:38:50,080
I heard some of the villagers say he never takes meals.

467
00:38:50,780 --> 00:38:52,580
He probably brought food with him.

468
00:38:53,880 --> 00:38:54,880
But what if he didn't?

469
00:38:55,480 --> 00:38:57,580
I'll bring him some rice balls, just in case.

470
00:38:58,580 --> 00:38:59,280
Good idea!

471
00:38:59,480 --> 00:39:00,280
I'll come too!

472
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:04,980
Can you keep a secret, Nezuko?

473
00:39:05,980 --> 00:39:08,680
Believe it or not, I'm getting hungry again!

474
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:11,180
It's probably from smelling the rice balls.

475
00:39:11,480 --> 00:39:12,780
Don't tell anyone, okay?

476
00:39:14,980 --> 00:39:17,980
Ms. Konroji, why'd you join the Demon Slayer Corps?

477
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:20,080
Oh, me?

478
00:39:21,080 --> 00:39:22,480
It's kind of embarrassing.

479
00:39:23,080 --> 00:39:24,480
I shouldn't say.

480
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:25,480
Or should I?

481
00:39:25,980 --> 00:39:26,880
Okay, fine.

482
00:39:27,580 --> 00:39:29,380
I joined hoping to find a man!

483
00:39:29,680 --> 00:39:31,880
What I could spend forever with!

484
00:39:32,280 --> 00:39:35,080
I mean, any girl would prefer someone who's stronger than her, right?

485
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:37,680
After all, we want to feel protected, you know what I mean?

486
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:39,980
Or maybe it's hard for a boy to understand.

487
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:43,580
I knew Hashiro were strong, so I thought one of them would be perfect!

488
00:39:43,980 --> 00:39:46,680
That's why I worked my hardest to become a Hashiro myself!

489
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:51,980
It looks like Genya isn't here.

490
00:39:52,780 --> 00:39:53,680
Lady Kanroji?

491
00:39:55,580 --> 00:39:57,880
I'm told they'll be done honing your swords soon.

492
00:39:58,680 --> 00:40:01,780
They've requested you come to the workshop to help make the final adjustments.

493
00:40:01,780 --> 00:40:06,180
Oh dear, it looks like I have to go now.

494
00:40:06,680 --> 00:40:09,180
If you'd like, we could take you.

495
00:40:09,680 --> 00:40:10,680
That's alright.

496
00:40:10,780 --> 00:40:12,680
I'll probably be leaving in the middle of the night.

497
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:15,380
Really?

498
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:15,980
But…

499
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:17,680
That makes sense.

500
00:40:20,180 --> 00:40:21,180
Thanks for offering.

501
00:40:22,480 --> 00:40:26,480
While we may not live to see each other ever again, let's give it our all.

502
00:40:26,480 --> 00:40:30,880
Never forget, you took on an upper-ranked demon and survived.

503
00:40:31,380 --> 00:40:32,880
That experience is priceless.

504
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:38,380
Training is valuable, but nothing can ever top what you learned from first-hand experience.

505
00:40:39,380 --> 00:40:42,380
I'd say what you all went through is equal to ten years of training.

506
00:40:43,380 --> 00:40:47,380
Whether you know it or not, Tanjiro, you're far stronger than you ever were before.

507
00:40:47,380 --> 00:40:52,280
Good luck, you two!

508
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:55,280
I'll be rooting for you every step of the way!

509
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:02,280
Thank you, Miss Kanroji.

510
00:41:02,280 --> 00:41:04,280
I've still got a ways to go.

511
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:07,280
After all, Mr. Uzui did everything.

512
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:13,280
I'll work even harder to defeat Muzan, Kibutsu-ji.

513
00:41:13,280 --> 00:41:21,180
Say, Tanjiro, you've been granted permission for a long stay, right?

514
00:41:21,180 --> 00:41:23,180
Uh, yes, I have.

515
00:41:28,180 --> 00:41:33,180
Well, apparently, there's a secret weapon in this village that will make you stronger.

516
00:41:33,180 --> 00:41:35,180
Try to find it, okay?

517
00:41:35,180 --> 00:41:37,180
Bye now!

518
00:41:37,180 --> 00:41:37,680
No!

519
00:41:59,080 --> 00:42:00,080
Wow!

520
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:03,580
This breakfast looks amazing!

521
00:42:04,080 --> 00:42:06,380
The vegetables were all picked on the mountainside here.

522
00:42:07,180 --> 00:42:09,880
And this fish was caught fresh from the river this morning.

523
00:42:10,680 --> 00:42:11,680
Really?

524
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:16,680
By the way, the Chief said he'll be contacting you as soon as they've found Mr. Haganezuka.

525
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:20,380
Until then, please build up your stamina and get some rest.

526
00:42:21,180 --> 00:42:21,680
Right!

527
00:42:21,980 --> 00:42:23,180
Thank you so much!

528
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:25,680
Thanks for the meal.

529
00:42:30,780 --> 00:42:32,380
Nezuko, you listening?

530
00:42:32,380 --> 00:42:37,880
I know I should focus on resting, but I can't stop thinking about it.

531
00:42:37,880 --> 00:42:39,880
What Ms. Konroji told me.

532
00:42:39,880 --> 00:42:43,880
How there's a secret weapon in the village that can make you stronger.

533
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:45,880
Want to look for it?

534
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:52,480
Wonder what kind of weapon it is?

535
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:57,980
Well, if it is a sword, maybe it's buried in the ground.

536
00:42:57,980 --> 00:42:59,980
It feels like we're on a treasure hunt, doesn't it?

537
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:06,980
While I do enjoy being here, the hot spring really reeks.

538
00:43:06,980 --> 00:43:12,480
Or my sense of smell is off, because I haven't recovered yet.

539
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:14,480
Ask all you want!

540
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:15,480
I'm not giving it to you!

541
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:19,480
I don't have time to argue with you.

542
00:43:19,480 --> 00:43:22,480
I came here for it, and I'm not leaving without it.

543
00:43:23,480 --> 00:43:24,480
A kid?

544
00:43:24,480 --> 00:43:25,480
And... is that...

545
00:43:26,480 --> 00:43:28,480
That's a Hashira, isn't it?

546
00:43:29,480 --> 00:43:31,480
What did Ms. Shinobu say his name was?

547
00:43:31,480 --> 00:43:32,980
I don't care if you're a Hashira or not!

548
00:43:32,980 --> 00:43:33,980
You're annoying!

549
00:43:33,980 --> 00:43:34,480
Alright!

550
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,480
So just leave!

551
00:43:35,480 --> 00:43:36,480
I missed Hashira.

552
00:43:36,980 --> 00:43:38,480
Muichiro Tokito.

553
00:43:39,980 --> 00:43:40,980
It is him.

554
00:43:41,480 --> 00:43:43,480
Just how many Hashira are here?

555
00:43:44,480 --> 00:43:45,480
Give me the key.

556
00:43:45,980 --> 00:43:46,980
In your dreams!

557
00:43:47,480 --> 00:43:49,980
My ancestor made this, and it's precious to me!

558
00:43:51,480 --> 00:43:51,980
Hold on.

559
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:53,980
Is someone else behind him?

560
00:43:54,980 --> 00:43:55,980
Didn't you hear me?

561
00:43:55,980 --> 00:43:57,980
I said I'm not giving it to you!

562
00:43:58,980 --> 00:44:00,480
There is.

563
00:44:00,980 --> 00:44:02,480
But... who is it?

564
00:44:03,480 --> 00:44:04,480
Do I know him?

565
00:44:08,480 --> 00:44:09,480
I do.

566
00:44:10,480 --> 00:44:12,480
I've seen that man before.

567
00:44:27,980 --> 00:44:29,480
much better than I've seen it.

568
00:44:29,480 --> 00:44:59,460
Thank you.

569
00:44:59,480 --> 00:45:29,460
Thank you.

570
00:45:29,480 --> 00:45:59,460
Thank you.

571
00:45:59,480 --> 00:46:29,460
Thank you.

572
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:59,460
Thank you.

573
00:46:59,480 --> 00:47:29,460
Thank you.

574
00:47:29,480 --> 00:47:59,460
Thank you.

575
00:47:59,480 --> 00:48:29,460
Thank you.

576
00:48:29,480 --> 00:48:59,440
Thank you.

577
00:48:59,440 --> 00:49:29,420
Thank you.

